if (IS_ERR(file)) {
    put_unused_fd(ufd);
    kfree(ctx);
    return ufd;
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because when `anon_inode_getfile()` fails, the code incorrectly returns the file descriptor `ufd` instead of an appropriate error code. This misleading return value suggests that the operation was successful, even though an error has occurred, leading to potential issues in the calling function.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
return PTR_ERR(file);
```
Reason:
The fix changes the return statement to `return PTR_ERR(file);`, which correctly returns the error code associated with the failure of `anon_inode_getfile()`. This ensures that the calling function receives the appropriate error indication, allowing it to handle the failure correctly.

